{"id":50242,"ord":36,"n_segments":142,"prev":50241,"next":50243,"doc":{"id":"66086","title":"66086_Zilner T. Randolph oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Zilner T. Randolph","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/66086/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66086"},"chapter":"Milwaukee with Bernie Young","title":"The Wisconsin Roof Garden and the Bernie Young band in Milwaukee","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"A white-clientele ballroom atop the Wisconsin Theater, Peacock's Alley, with a white band and Bernie Young's band billed as Creoles.","period":"c. 1926","year_from":1926,"year_to":1926,"words":132,"start":[51,2],"end":[52,6],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=66086#s50242","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Milwaukee","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"Wisconsin Avenue","focus":0,"type":"street","in":"Milwaukee"}],"venues":[{"name":"Wisconsin Roof Garden","focus":1,"city":"Milwaukee"},{"name":"Peacock's Alley","focus":1,"city":"Milwaukee"},{"name":"Wisconsin Theater","focus":0,"city":"Milwaukee"}],"bands":[{"name":"Bernie Young's band","focus":1,"leader":"Bernie Young"}]},"people":[{"name":"Bernie Young","qid":"Q19275122","n":1},{"name":"Eddie Inge","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":37,"theme_name":"Gangsters, bootleggers and rough clubs of Prohibition","community":74,"community_name":"Cabarets, honky-tonks and the Storyville nightlife scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":51,"b":2,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Well, you took the job in Milwaukee and that was the -- what was -- the Wisconsin --"},{"p":51,"b":3,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Wisconsin Roof Garden. Two bands."},{"p":51,"b":4,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Was that a ballroom?"},{"p":51,"b":5,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Ballroom. And what a ballroom. They had a place called Peacock's Alley and that's -- that was one of the prettiest places you want to see in your life."},{"p":51,"b":6,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Was this downtown?"},{"p":51,"b":7,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Yeah, on Wisconsin Avenue, right downtown. Atop of the Wisconsin Theater."},{"p":51,"b":8,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"I see. Then, the clientele was white?"},{"p":51,"b":9,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"All white, yes, all white."},{"p":51,"b":10,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"And were both bands black?"},{"p":52,"b":0,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"No, no, white and colored band."},{"p":52,"b":1,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"I see. Now, Ed Inge --"},{"p":52,"b":2,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Well, it's a funny thing. We weren't supposed to be just a black band. We were supposed to be Creoles."},{"p":52,"b":3,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Oh, I see."},{"p":52,"b":4,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"(unintelligible)."},{"p":52,"b":5,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Who had the band?"},{"p":52,"b":6,"s":"MR. RANDOLPH","x":"Bernie Young had the band."}]}